  "elementId" : "rich_text_1",
  "elementLabel" : "Rich text 1",
  "propertyValues" : {
    "html" : {
      "type" : "TRANSLATION_LITERAL",
      "value" : {
        "code" : null,
        "message" : "<p>The <strong>stale series ratio</strong> is a measure of the percentage of series that haven't had a value published to them for a specified number of days. This day value is 7 days by default but is configurable. The closer this value is to 0%, the less unused series there are.</p>\n<p>The&nbsp;<strong>data utilization efficiency</strong> is the percentage of datapoints per metric that have a non-null value. The closer this value is to 100%, the fewer null datapoints there are.</p>\n<p>The&nbsp;<strong>average unutilized data gap</strong> is the average gap between two non-null data points. It provides a snapshot as to how frequently values are being published to the server. If this value is moderately large, it may signify that you are using the wrong schedule, and not utilizing the available data efficiently.</p>",
        "comment" : ""
      }
    }
  },
